A||||8||GT Bastard||Is the 4sp diff between 4&6 cyl motors?||||5||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-25-2000||01:53 PM||||I've heard that there is a difference in the bell-housing on 4cyl trannys....  Is this true?||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||03-25-2000||08:07 PM||||The bolt patterns are the same. The V6 tranny is a little more built up than the 4 cyl tranny to handle a little more torque.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||03-25-2000||08:47 PM||||Has anybody tried putting the 4cyl tranny on a 6cyl car with good results?  How do you mean, built?  thanks for your info.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||HF6582||03-25-2000||09:20 PM||||There are no differances in the 4spds offered for the the 4 or 6 cylinder. If you check all part numbers they are the same. The only thing that is differant is gear ratios.<P>Also, if you go back to the '80's the super duty program was using <B> all GM parts except for the gears </B>.<P>Webster gears provided hardend gears in all differant ratios.<P>Scott  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||03-25-2000||09:30 PM||||thanks for the info....  I've heard all kinds of different responses from people.  How does the 4sp rate as a performance tranny?  I've never driven a Getrag or a 4sp v6 Fiero before.   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||03-25-2000||09:39 PM||||I use to have an 86 V-6 with 4spd and the nice thing was second gear was a great gear!<BR>I have not driven a getreg but I did like the 4spd. Just a little high rpm wise at highway speeds but as for 0-60 it was good. I have heard the getreg was more balanced with it's gear ratio's.||||reg||1
Z||000006||HF6582||03-25-2000||10:22 PM||||It really depends on your usage. If it is a daily drive over moderate distance I would use a five speed. <P>From all of the info that I have gathered, GM considered the gears to be to weak for racing, but for the street they should be fine. I have a M19 4spd that is going in my 86GT. I am not worried about the durability, because I don't think that it will be an issue for my street car.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||03-26-2000||11:38 PM||||After consulting the 22P catalog I would have to say that I appear to be wrong about the cases being different. This being said I would still have to wonder why the trannys that we have pulled off of the V6 that were originally from 84 powertrains (designation MY8/M19) were prone to failure as opposed to having a tranny from the correct year (designation MY8/M17). I stand corrected but still puzzled.||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT Bastard||03-26-2000||11:58 PM||||WKD.... Thanks for responding to my question anyways.  I'm not confused anymore!  ||||reg||1
